[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Technical Tutorial: Securing Azure Workloads with Microsoft Entra ID, Conditional Access, and Identity Protection"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"In modern cloud architecture, identity is the new security perimeter. Securing your Azure environment requires transitioning from traditional network-based security to a robust, identity-centric zero trust model. This tutorial covers the integration of Microsoft Entra ID (formerly Azure Active Directory), Conditional Access Policies, and Microsoft Entra ID Protection to safeguard your cloud resources."},{"order":3,"type":"heading","text":"Prerequisites"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"An active Microsoft Azure subscription with a Microsoft Entra ID P2 license (required for Identity Protection and risk-based policies)."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Global Administrator or Conditional Access Administrator role assigned to your account."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Azure CLI installed locally or access to the Azure Cloud Shell."},{"order":7,"type":"heading","text":"Step 1: Configuring Microsoft Entra ID Baseline Security"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"Before implementing Conditional Access, you must ensure that multi-factor authentication (MFA) is registered for all users and security defaults are properly managed. While Security Defaults offer basic protection, enterprises typically disable them to implement granular Conditional Access Policies."},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"az login
az account set --subscription "YOUR_SUBSCRIPTION_ID""},{"order":10,"type":"heading","text":"Step 2: Implementing Risk-Based Policies via Identity Protection"},{"order":11,"type":"paragraph","text":"Microsoft Entra ID Protection uses heuristics and machine learning to detect potential compromises to your identities. You can configure user risk and sign-in risk policies to automatically remediate threats."},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"Enabling User Risk Policy"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"Navigate to the Microsoft Entra admin center, select Protection, and then Identity Protection. Click on 'User risk policy'. Set the assignments to include all users and configure the condition to 'High' risk. Set the access control to 'Allow access' but require a password change."},{"order":14,"type":"heading","text":"Step 3: Creating a Conditional Access Policy"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"Conditional Access policies act as if-then statements: if a user wants to access a resource, they must complete an action. Below is a conceptual implementation of a policy that enforces MFA for all cloud apps when sign-in risk is detected as medium or high."},{"order":16,"type":"code","text":"{
  "displayName": "Require MFA for Risky Sign-ins",
  "state": "enabled",
  "conditions": {
    "signInRiskLevels": ["medium", "high"],
    "applications": {
      "includeApplications": ["All"]
    }
  },
  "grantControls": {
    "operator": "AND",
    "grantControls": ["mfa"]
  }
}"},{"order":17,"type":"heading","text":"Step 4: Using Microsoft Graph API to Audit Conditional Access Policies"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"Administrators can use the Microsoft Graph API to programmatically list and verify active Conditional Access policies in their tenant to ensure compliance."},{"order":19,"type":"code","text":"GET https://graph.microsoft.com/v1.0/identity/conditionalAccess/policies"},{"order":20,"type":"heading","text":"Best Practices and Conclusion"},{"order":21,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always use 'Report-only' mode when deploying new Conditional Access policies to evaluate impact before enforcement."},{"order":22,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Exclude at least one break-glass (Emergency Access) account from your Conditional Access policies to prevent lockout."},{"order":23,"type":"paragraph","text":"By combining Microsoft Entra ID, Identity Protection, and Conditional Access, organizations can dynamically evaluate risk and apply least-privilege access controls across all Azure resources."}]
